SYNCEDPLAYBACKDECKLINK

This project plays back 8 video files on a decklink quad card.
On the Interface, the user must select the root directory containing sessions.

The Folder structure must be as follows:

Root Dir/
    |---Session 1/
        |---Playlist 1/
            |---Video1.mp4
            |---Video2.mp4
            |---Video2.mp4
            |---Video2.mp4
            |---Video2.mp4
            |---Video2.mp4
    |---Session 2/
        |---Playlist 1/
            |---Video1.mp4
            |---Video2.mp4
            |---Video2.mp4
            |---Video2.mp4
            |---Video2.mp4
            |---Video2.mp4


Controls:
    Keyboard Keys:
        A - Previous
        Z - Next
        Space - Pause/Play

Channel Mapping:
    Decklink Device 1 = Channel 1
    Decklink Device 2 = Channel 2
    Decklink Device 3 = Channel 3
    Decklink Device 4 = Channel 4
    Decklink Device 5 = Channel 5
    Decklink Device 6 = Channel 6
    Decklink Device 7 = Channel 7
    Decklink Device 8 = Channel 8


Note: The application Requires that there be decklink drivers installed as it does not
come with the driver pre-packaged. 

Note: The decklink devices must be set to Half-duplex mode (SDI1->Device 1)
and not full-duplex mode (SDI10>Device1&Device2)